      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-09_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>PRETTY HAT.</head>
        <p>A PRETTY HAT.</p>
        <p>underneath the elegant little coat. The wide hat of brown rustic straw, fashioned by hand, is trimmed with creamy lace which also falls in the fashionable curtain at the back. Under the brim some pale pink and cream roses and buds nestle. Nothing could be smarter for immediate wear than such a toilette as brown is one of the most fashionable colours, and in a golden shade is even used for evening wear as it is found to light up well. Indeed, there are many tones of colour pressed into service for evening wear and which form very striking and effective gowns, which have hitherto been solely daylight colours, but are now discovered to be wonderfully becoming to certain com- plexions seen under the blaze of electric lights. The pretty hat which forms the subject of my second sketch is expressed in pastel green straw of a dull soft tone into which a greyish shade is somehow introduced. The roses are full blown gloire de dijon with their soft creamy petals and pinkish yellow hearts, and are wonderfully natural-looking. Indeed, it is really marvellous to what perfection the manufacture of artificial flowers has been developed, and it is difficult to believe that it is not in truth the real work of Nature that we are looking upon. The tints and shapes of petal and leaf are copied faithfully and it is only by touch that one can discover the red from the imitation flower. A soft drapery of fine lace is further used to trim this hat and after passing round the crown it falls to the shoulders in a cache peigne. Indeed this</p>
        <p>,-4 ' , • '_'_----- ''- .-- _.,, , --g4.!,,, I pile ~,jokk silfo,4t; ' , . TIT, . . ;ra - ii; 'I, VI) N .., 41, lii .. :/ f,, A \e, • -11111114 11 •,,,wr, ~ ~ • , ii 1, ,</p>
