      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-09_WidnesExaminer_art0078" n="art0078">
        <head>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL. " Ungrateful Sankey."</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL. " Ungrateful Sankey."</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL</p>
        <p>" Observer" Cup Final.</p>
        <p>SUTTON COMMERCIAL THE VICTORS.</p>
        <p>The final meeting of this Council as at present con- stituted was held at Bewsey Chambers on Wednesday The hopes of the Thelwall team to retain the afternoon under the presidency of Mr. T. Halton. There " Observer " cup for a second year were doomed to dis- were also present :—Messrs. Brooks, Houghton, Back- appointment, for the final on Saturday resulted in a house, Longton, Mather, J. C. Sutton (clerk), S. Sutton victory for Sutton Commercial. Despite the wretched (deputy clerk), B. S. Newcombe (surveyor), H. H. weather, the great interest taken in the encounter was Burnage (assistant surveyor), and F. Kerfoot (inspector reflected man attendance of 2,000 spectators. The ser- of nuisances.) vices of Mr. J. Lewis, of Blackburn, the well-known in- THE ESTIMATES. ternational referee, had been secured, and the teams The Cherix produced the estimates of expenditure for lined up as follows :—Thelwall : Smith,goal ; Strettle the ensuing half year, and recommended a call upon the and Short, backs; Howard, Lowndes and Blackshaw, townships for general expenses at the rate of sd. in the half backs ; Riley,Price, S. Woods, ClWoods,and Green, .2, as against 6d. for the past half year, and 6d. for the forwards. Sutton Commercial: Scott, goal; Cox and corresponding half of last year. The special calls upon Williams, backs; Tinsley, Taylor and Lewis, half backs; the separate townships would be :--Burtonwood, £80; Dean, Hand, Wilson, Hewitt and Hill, forwards. The Penketh, £80; Poulton, £4O; Rirton, £3O; Great game was keenly contested from the outset, but Sankey, £3O. Sutton quickly became aggressive and Band scored Mr. Baooxs moved that the calls he made as recom- in fine style. Sutton were penalized and C. Wood mended by the Clerk. It seemed to be the general landed a goal for the" city." Both tennis worked bard fashion to raise the rates, and he was very glad they but there was no further scoring before the interval. were able to make an exception. He thought it desi