      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-09_WidnesExaminer_art0095" n="art0095">
        <head>GORDON-BENNETT MOTOR RACE.</head>
        <p>THE GORDON-BENNETT MOTOR RACE.</p>
        <p>Since its institution, the race for the Gordon-Bennett trophy has each year grown in popularity, until now it is one of the international sporting events of the year. Last year it was won for Germany by Herr jenatzy on a Mercedes car: so, under the conditions of the race, this year it will be held in that country. The course has been chosen, and is pronounced by experts to be an admirable one, and the best used so for in the history of the race in many respects, but it is very hilly all the way, which will militate against good times. However, the roads are wide and the surface is good, and there are no very bad turnings as in Ireland last year. The course is situated near Frankfort, and the starting-point will be at Kasten - Saalburg, near Homburg, tae dis- tance altogether heing very nearly 340</p>
