      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-09_WidnesExaminer_art0096" n="art0096">
        <head>COURSE OF THE GORDON-BENNETT RACE,</head>
        <p>THE COURSE OF THE GORDON-BENNETT RACE,</p>
        <p>miles. Immense interest is being displayed in it by motorists of all countries; and a new country is entering the lists in Italy, which will be represented by three "Fiat cars. In the United Kingdom the elimi- nating trials for the English team were impossible without a special Act of Parlia- ment, and at one time it was thought that they would have to be held abroad; but it has now been arranged to hold them in the Isle of Man, where a suitable course has been selected and is being prepared. The race itself takes place on i7th, and it is expect?' that many Tole will De present;</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-09_WidnesExaminer_art0097" n="art0097">
        <head>TRIBUTE TO THE IRISH LANGUAGE.</head>
        <p>A TRIBUTE TO THE IRISH LANGUAGE.</p>
        <p>In the course of a speech at the Trish Teachers' Con- gress at Belfast on Wednesday, Mr. Dolan, a Southern delegate, said the Irish language had ithree great qual- itiesto recommend it. All who knew it considered it was the language in which they could pray most fer- vently, curse the most bitterly and court the most sweetly. (1..0ud laughter):</p>
