        <p>DROWNING CASE.—An inquest was held at Stockton Heath, Warrington, on Friday, on Charles William Clark, four years of age, son of Jane Clarke. staying at Dingle Lodge, Appleton, whose husband has gone to 'fish- Canada. Deceased, with two other boys, was playin near a sticks, t g afetlln Appleton, and, in trying to get some in g. John Clayton, a farm labourer work- ingst near, Was alarmed, but the child was dead when got out of the water.—Verdict, " Accidentally drowned."</p>
